<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_LongShade.xml                 UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-24
  ============================================================================

  Puts the campaign's Long Shade fauna roster onto RM_LongShade, adding onto the
  native creatures src/RimMandrake/LongShade/Defs/BiomeDefs/RM_LongShade.xml
  ships on its own (JOE_Landopus, and RM_Qorrax whose def lives in mandrake.rm.stillsand). The Star Wars cast reaches
  RM_LongShade HERE, never in the LongShade mod itself — same shape as
  WildAnimals_Greentide.xml / WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml.

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. §7 Q11 (owner, 2026-09-22): "RimMandrake should not
  name star wars ever." So RM_LongShade may not carry this cast, and at Phase B of
  design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md the RUT_Desert def that currently
  carries it dies and RM_LongShade takes the tiles.

  🔴 LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 (2026-09-27 sitting) REWROTE this file's Add
  block — do not trust any older doc's row count against it. Starting from the
  52-row state (51 original transplant + RSW_GlitterBird):
    - 14 invented-name rows LEFT this file for good (Q1, ratified) — bokka,
      ossik, kudda, thurra, vosska, khorrak, ommok, ulgga, jellypot, truffle
      mole, great devourer, groundrunner, mature fleshbeast, shade whale. They
      are now inline RM_ defs on RM_LongShade itself
      (RM_LongShade_Fauna.xml / RM_LongShade_Gloomcast.xml), same weights.
    - RSW_Kreetle and RSW_Gizka LEFT this file's Add block entirely (Q6) —
      kreetle's one home is now the Stillsand (this doc's own §7 Q6
      recommendation was reversed by the card), gizka's is Pyrelands+Stillsand
      per the pre-existing 2026-09-14 ruling. Neither is wired to the Long
      Shade by any route any more.
    - RSW_Dewback went IN (Q8): herd/mount stock, canon Star Wars (Tatooine
      native, mlie.starwarsanimalcollection absorption) so it stays in this
      Utinni layer rather than moving tiers — the ruling was BIOME WIRING, not
      a tier move. Predator flag MEASURED: RSW_Dewback.xml's own <race> block
      carries NO <predator> node at all, so it already defaults false — the
      roster's "flag noise" suspicion is confirmed correct, no def edit
      needed. Slowed under the pursuit ban, same wraid/gutkurr treatment:
      moveSpeed 4.7 -> 4.4 via a new rosters/desert.json stat_adjustments row,
      regenerated into BiomeFaunaStatAdjustments_Generated.xml (never hand-
      edit that file directly). Blurrg stays OUT — its home is the Leaning
      Scrub sitting, not here.
  Net: 35 canon rows (51 original minus the 14 that tier-moved minus Kreetle
  and Gizka) + RSW_Dewback = 36 rows in the Add block below (MEASURED via
  python xml.etree against this file as written). RSW_GlitterBird, which stood
  here unaffected by the 2026-09-27 sitting, LEFT this file at
  LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1 part 4 — merged into the inline RM_Pirrik.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH (AT AUTHORING, 2026-09-24, since amended above): every
  surviving weight below is a verbatim copy of the original transplant off
  Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_Desert.xml's own wildAnimals block — nothing rescaled.

  Unlike WildAnimals_Greentide.xml, there is NO PatchOperationReplace here:
  RM_LongShade does not ship a Core-only placeholder roster to swap out — its
  native rows are the biome's real content and stay put. This file is
  Add-only, same shape as WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml's second block.

  🔴 OUR DEFS, NOT THE DONOR'S. Owner ruling 2026-09-19, verbatim: "They should be
  using OUR creatures, not the donor references. The donor references, if any,
  should never be used again." Every row below is already this repo's own RSW_
  port — nothing here casts a donor's bare defName.

  ============================================================================
  KNOWN OPEN QUESTIONS — carried from the item, not resolved here
  ============================================================================

  1. roster row AA_SandLion (0.5, "sand burrower swimmer") has no wired def row
     — CONFIRMED DEAD 2026-09-27 (LONGSHADE_DESIGN_SITTING_1 Q9): the ported
     RSW_SandLion (vekka) lives in the Stillsand, its one home. Nothing to fix
     here; desert.json's homeless-reserve entry already records this
     correctly, checked this pass (LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1).
  2. def row RSW_Stoneback (0.5) is wired here (per the frozen twin) but
     absent from rosters/desert.json — the roster file is stale by this
     addition, not this file. Unaffected by this pass (not part of the 14
     tier-move rows, still SW-tier).

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing — PatchOperationConditional returns
  true on no match, and an unmatched PatchOperationAdd is silent. A clean
  validate_patch.py run is NOT proof a row landed. 🔴 UNVERIFIED AGAINST A LOAD:
  authored offline this pass too (LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1) — no bridge/def-
  dump confirmation of the 38-row Add block or the inline 14-row move.
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- The remaining 38 rows: 36 canon Star Wars + the whale's commensal +
       Dewback, all OUR OWN RSW_ defs (never the donor's bare names).
       Add-only: RM_LongShade's own wildAnimals node already carries its 16
       native/tier-moved rows, guarded on the target node rather than on a
       donor so this is a silent no-op if mandrake.rm.longshade is ever not
       loaded. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods><li>RimMandrake: SW — Bestiary</li></mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_LongShade"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_LongShade"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
        <value>
          <RSW_Bantha>0.8</RSW_Bantha>
          <RSW_Shyrack>0.6</RSW_Shyrack>
          <RSW_Gorg>0.4</RSW_Gorg>
          <RSW_Gutkurr>0.4</RSW_Gutkurr>
          <RSW_Jamel>0.4</RSW_Jamel>
          <RSW_LongtailGorg>0.4</RSW_LongtailGorg>
          <RSW_Ronto>0.4</RSW_Ronto>
          <RSW_Sketto>0.8</RSW_Sketto>
          <RSW_Wraid>0.4</RSW_Wraid>
          <RSW_WraidAlpha>0.15</RSW_WraidAlpha>
          <RSW_Eopie>0.3</RSW_Eopie>
          <RSW_Hrumph>0.3</RSW_Hrumph>
          <RSW_IridonianReek>0.3</RSW_IridonianReek>
          <RSW_Jimvu>0.3</RSW_Jimvu>
          <RSW_Kwi>0.3</RSW_Kwi>
          <RSW_Skalder>0.3</RSW_Skalder>
          <RSW_Uvak>0.3</RSW_Uvak>
          <RSW_Varactyl>0.3</RSW_Varactyl>
          <RSW_Zeer>0.3</RSW_Zeer>
          <RSW_Falumpaset>0.2</RSW_Falumpaset>
          <RSW_FrilledGorg>0.2</RSW_FrilledGorg>
          <RSW_Jakobeast>0.2</RSW_Jakobeast>
          <RSW_Nerf>0.2</RSW_Nerf>
          <RSW_Nuna>0.2</RSW_Nuna>
          <RSW_Shaak>0.2</RSW_Shaak>
          <RSW_TeeMuss>0.2</RSW_TeeMuss>
          <RSW_Worrt>0.2</RSW_Worrt>
          <RSW_Bolotaur>0.1</RSW_Bolotaur>
          <RSW_Clodhopper>0.1</RSW_Clodhopper>
          <RSW_FeralGrazer>0.1</RSW_FeralGrazer>
          <RSW_Iriaz>0.1</RSW_Iriaz>
          <RSW_Krykna>0.1</RSW_Krykna>
          <RSW_Runyip>0.1</RSW_Runyip>
          <RSW_Voorpak>0.05</RSW_Voorpak>
          <RSW_Horax>0.01</RSW_Horax>
          <!-- LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1 part 4: RSW_GlitterBird REMOVED from
               this Add block — it and the sitting's own "pirrik" filler were one
               creature (Q11a: "glitter-bird" is descriptive English, not canon
               Star Wars IP, so it belongs in the RM_ tier, not here). Merged
               into RM_Pirrik, now inline on RM_LongShade itself alongside the
               biome's other invented-name rows, carrying the same
               RM_ShadowFollowerExtension wiring. See RM_LongShade_Fillers.xml. -->
          <!-- LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q8: Dewback IN as herd/mount stock.
               moveSpeed slowed 4.7->4.4 via rosters/desert.json
               stat_adjustments (BiomeFaunaStatAdjustments_Generated.xml), not
               here — this weight is unaffected by that separate patch. -->
          <RSW_Dewback>0.3</RSW_Dewback>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- SW_FAUNA_NEVER_IN_RM_TIER_1, 2026-09-25: the wildPlants rows moved out
       of RM_LongShade.xml (see that file's own header for what was found and
       why). LONGSHADE_RULED_CONTENT_1 Q2 then moved RSW_Ultracactus back OUT
       of this list — it is inline again, this time correctly as RM_Ultracactus
       (Q2: "not canon, I made it"). Add-only: RM_LongShade's own wildPlants
       node already carries its 5 native/tier-moved rows, same shape as Op 1
       above. Weights unchanged from what this file carried before. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods><li>RimMandrake: SW — Bestiary</li></mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_LongShade"]/wildPlants</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_LongShade"]/wildPlants</xpath>
        <value>
          <RSW_SurraGrass>0.6</RSW_SurraGrass>
          <RSW_Plant_Chakroot_Wild>0.3</RSW_Plant_Chakroot_Wild>
          <RSW_Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild>0.2</RSW_Plant_HubbaGourd_Wild>
          <RSW_VellaraBloom>0.12</RSW_VellaraBloom>
          <RSW_DommoTree>0.06</RSW_DommoTree>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
